    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314-a2">

                <pb facs="0800" n="1430" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg1430"/>

                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to the communication which you
                    were pleased to address to me under date of the 19th ultimo, I have the honor to
                    inform you that, according to article 13 of the constitution of the grand duchy,
                    citizenship is acquired— <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>By birth, for those whose father or mother are at that time Hessian
                            subjects.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>By marriage, for a foreign woman who marries a Hessian subject.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>By appointment to a public office.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>By special admission.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Consequently, children born in the grand ducal territory of foreign parents are
                    regarded as foreigners until they have acquired Hessian nationality by one of
                    the means above mentioned.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BARON VON DALWIGK.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Darmstadt</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1868-09-07"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 7,
                        1868</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
